<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>LeadIntel AI — <%= screen.name %></title>
<%# Fonts and icons are served from /assets, not from fonts.googleapis.com and
    unpkg.com. Three render-blocking stylesheets across two extra origins used
    to sit ahead of the first paint here, each paying its own DNS, TCP and TLS
    before it started; measured from Kerala they cost ~260ms, ~280ms and ~370ms
    against a server that answers the page in ~100ms. See the notes at the top
    of inter.css and phosphor.css. %>
<%# Declared, so the browser stops probing /favicon.ico — which this app has
    never had. Every page load spent a request on it and logged a 404 in the
    console, and the 404 page it reached is the one the note further down
    explains had to be taught to render without a screen behind it. %>
<link rel="icon" href="<%= asset('favicon.svg') %>" type="image/svg+xml">
<%# Preloaded at the literal path inter.css asks for, with no ?v= on it. The
    fingerprint helper would produce a *different* URL from the one inside the
    stylesheet, and a browser treats those as two fonts: the preload fetched
    47KB and then the stylesheet fetched the same 47KB again. Fonts are busted
    by renaming the file, which is what swapping a typeface means anyway. %>
<link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/Inter-latin.f11d729b.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('inter.css') %>">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('phosphor.css') %>">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('nocturne.css') %>">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('app.css') %>">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('hover.css') %>">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('app-ui.css') %>">
</head>
<body>

<%
/* A skip link, because the sidebar is thirteen focusable items before the
   content starts and a keyboard user should not have to walk past them on
   every screen. Visible only when focused. */
%>
<a class="li-skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<div class="app">

  <%- include('partials/sidebar', shell) %>

  <div class="main-col">
    <%- include('partials/topbar', shell) %>
    <%- include('partials/filterbar', shell) %>

    <main id="main" tabindex="-1" aria-label="<%= screen.name %>">
      <%- include('app/attribution-preview', { attrPreview: attrPreview }) %>
      <%- include('app/filter-note', { filterNote: filterNote }) %>
      <%
      /* A screen the design does not define — Connections is ours, not the
         design's, so its markup lives in views/app/ and the converter never
         touches it. */
      %>
      <% if (screen.app) { %>
        <%- include('app/' + screen.app, data || {}) %>
      <% } else if (hasView) { %>
        <%- include('screens/' + screen.view, data || {}) %>
      <% } else { %>
        <div style="max-width:620px; margin:64px auto; text-align:center;">
          <i class="<%= screen.icon %>" style="font-size:30px; color:var(--color-neutral-700);"></i>
          <h2 style="margin:14px 0 6px; font-size:19px; font-weight:500;"><%= screen.name %></h2>
          <p style="font-size:12.5px; color:var(--color-neutral-500); line-height:1.6;">
            No view generated for this screen yet.
          </p>
        </div>
      <% } %>
    </main>
  </div>

  <% if (drawer) { %>
    <%- include('screens/overlay-creative-detail', drawer.data) %>
  <% } %>

</div>

<%- include('app/palette', { palette: palette }) %>
<%- include('app/notifications', { notifications: notifications }) %>

<script type="application/json" id="li-filter-data"><%- JSON.stringify(filterData) %></script>
<%# A screen may offer rankings the design drew a caret for and no menu. The
    options travel here so the control can build one at runtime, rather than
    the markup being written into views/screens/, which the converter owns. %>
<%# `data` is null on the not-found page, which has no screen behind it and so
    has nothing to sort or judge by. Reading through it threw, and the throw
    replaced every 404 with a 500 — a mistyped URL, a link that moved, and
    /favicon.ico, which the browser asks for on every single page load. %>
<script type="application/json" id="li-sort-data"><%- JSON.stringify((data && data.sortOptions) || []) %></script>
<%# What the screen judges by — different businesses buy against different
    measures, and this one buys against qualified lead CPL. %>
<script type="application/json" id="li-goal-data"><%- JSON.stringify((data && data.goalOptions) || []) %></script>
<%# Who is signed in, for the profile menu. The avatar can carry initials and
    a title and no more; the menu needs the role, the workspace and what the
    role may actually do. %>
<script type="application/json" id="li-me-data"><%- JSON.stringify(shell.me || null) %></script>
<script type="application/json" id="li-notif-count"><%- JSON.stringify({ count: notifications.count }) %></script>

<script src="<%= asset('actions.js') %>"></script>
<script src="<%= asset('app-ui.js') %>"></script>
<%# The phone top bar. Its own file so a throw in it cannot take the palette,
    the chips and the range menu down with it. %>
<script src="<%= asset('mobile-topbar.js') %>"></script>
</body>
</html>
